---
import Layout from "../../Base.astro";
import SimpleHero from "../../components/SimpleHero.astro";
import FeaturedArticles from "../../components/FeaturedArticles.astro";
import ServicesRelatedWork from "../../components/ServicesRelatedWork.astro";
import "../../styles/pages/_services-list.scss";
---

<Layout
  title="Ecommerce Website Development &amp; Integrations | Kelp"
  description="Kelp builds Shopify and WooCommerce stores for complex catalogs, custom products, conversion, and connections to the systems behind every order."
>
  <SimpleHero
    tagline="Ecommerce Development"
    title="Ecommerce That Actually Converts"
    description="Selling online isn’t just about having a store—it’s about removing friction from every step of the buying process. We build ecommerce systems that are fast, intuitive, and designed to turn traffic into revenue."
    lottieFile="ecommerce.json"
  />

  <div
    class="wrapper wrapper--narrow"
    style="padding-bottom: 100px; text-align: center;"
  >
    We are certified partners with both
    <a href="https://woocommerce.com/development-services/kelp-creative-agency/232621912/">
      WooCommerce
    </a>
    and Shopify.
  </div>

  <div class="service-body">
    <div class="wrapper wrapper--narrow">
      <h2>Where most ecommerce sites fall short</h2>
      <p>
        Most ecommerce sites don’t fail because of their products—they fail
        because of friction. Slow load times, confusing navigation, broken
        checkout flows, and disconnected systems all contribute to lost revenue.
      </p>
      <p>
        A customer who is ready to buy should never have to think about how your
        site works. When the experience is unclear or inefficient, they leave.
      </p>

      <h2>What we focus on</h2>
      <p>
        We treat ecommerce as a system, not just a storefront. Every part of the
        experience—from product discovery to checkout—should work together to
        support a single goal: conversion.
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li>Clear product structure and navigation</li>
        <li>Fast, performance-focused builds</li>
        <li>Optimized cart and checkout experiences</li>
        <li>
          Seamless integrations with payment, shipping, and inventory systems
        </li>
        <li>Scalable platforms that grow with your business</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How we approach it</h2>
      <p>
        We start by understanding how your business sells—then build the system
        to support it.
      </p>

      <ol>
        <li>
          <strong>Define the buying journey:</strong> Identify how customers
          discover, evaluate, and purchase your products.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Structure the store:</strong> Organize products, categories,
          and content to reduce friction and improve clarity.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Design for conversion:</strong> Create layouts and
          interactions that guide users toward purchase.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Build and integrate:</strong> Develop the store and connect it
          to the tools that power your operations.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Refine and optimize:</strong> Continuously improve
          performance, usability, and conversion rates over time.
        </li>
      </ol>

      <h2>The outcome</h2>
      <p>
        A well-built ecommerce system removes friction, increases conversion
        rates, and gives your business a foundation that can scale without
        constant rework.
      </p>

      <h2>Make Complex Products Easier to Buy</h2>
      <p>
        We organize catalogs so customers can find the right product, compare
        options, understand specifications, and complete the purchase. That can
        mean better categories and filters, clearer product pages, a custom
        configurator, a B2B quote path, or a checkout that removes avoidable
        steps. The design should fit the way the business actually sells.
      </p>
      <h2>Connect the Systems Behind Each Order</h2>
      <p>
        We can scope integrations for POS, inventory, ERP, shipping and
        fulfillment, customer records, B2B pricing, product information, and
        custom production software. The first question is where each piece of
        data should live. The next is how updates, exceptions, and failures
        should be handled. A good integration plan covers what happens when a
        SKU changes, an order is edited, stock is unavailable, or one system is
        temporarily down.
      </p>
      <h2>Choose the Platform That Fits the Workflow</h2>
      <p>
        Kelp works with Shopify and WooCommerce. A conventional Shopify
        storefront may be the right fit; a custom theme or Hydrogen build may
        serve a more demanding experience. WooCommerce can offer flexibility for
        workflows that need deeper customization. We evaluate product rules,
        staff processes, and integration requirements before committing to a
        platform.
      </p>
      <h2>Proven Work for a Nonstandard Order Flow</h2>
      <p>
        <a href="/work/us-labels/">US Labels</a> needed a responsive custom label designer and a way to send
        orders to Windows printing software. Kelp selected WooCommerce for the
        use case and built a Node.js and Express API service to connect the
        store with production. The result is a useful example of why a store
        should be designed around the full order path, not only the product
        grid.
      </p>
      <p>
        A better store helps shoppers choose with confidence and gives staff an
        order they can actually fulfill. Clear catalog information, dependable
        data flow, and a considered checkout reduce confusion on both sides. The
        right implementation also leaves the team able to manage products and
        respond when requirements change.
      </p>
      <p>
        AI-driven shopping will make accurate product information and clear
        pages more important. We help clients prepare the catalog, storefront,
        and systems that support that information; no agency can guarantee
        placement in an AI shopping response. If your store is losing sales or
        creating manual work, show us the workflow and we will help identify
        what needs design, development, or integration. For a first website
        snapshot, use the free <a href="/website-checker/">Website Checker</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        Show us a typical order and one order that causes problems. Those
        examples reveal more about the build than a feature list and help us
        scope the storefront and integrations accurately.
      </p>
      <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      <h3>Can Kelp work with our current ecommerce platform?</h3>
      <p>
        Often. We review what the platform can support, what can be improved
        through configuration or development, and where a change of platform may
        be justified.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href="/contact/" class="button button--green">
          Start a Project
        </a>
      </p>
    </div>

    <ServicesRelatedWork tag={84} />
  </div>

  <FeaturedArticles />
</Layout>
